  <property name="kdenlive:clipname">BigTXT1</property>
  <property name="xmldata">&lt;kdenlivetitle LC_NUMERIC="C" duration="900" height="720" out="899" width="1280">
 &lt;item type="QGraphicsTextItem" z-index="0">
  &lt;position x="20" y="20">
   &lt;transform rotation="0,0,0" zoom="100">1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1&lt;/transform>
  &lt;/position>
  &lt;content alignment="1" box-height="779" box-width="859.547" font="DejaVu Serif" font-color="255,255,255,255" font-italic="0" font-pixel-size="35" font-underline="0" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="0" line-spacing="0" shadow="0;#64000000;3;3;3" tab-width="80" typewriter="0;1;1;0;0">Outside the city walls, the danger doesn't
come only from the local wildlife. The wind,
which may look like a simple sandstorm,
causes partial paralysis of the human body.

Simply looking around becomes difficult;
jumping becomes impossible, as does
crouching. Moving your arms is not
restricted.

You only need to breathe this air for two
minutes to experience the negative effects
described earlier. And that is already fatal.

The Hoyploma Health Department, in
collaboration with local law enforcement,
is actively working to prevent citizens from
leaving the city without authorization and
proper equipment.&lt;/content>
 &lt;/item>
 &lt;startviewport rect="0,-740,1280,720"/>
 &lt;endviewport rect="0,100,1280,720"/>
 &lt;background color="0,0,0,0"/>
&lt;/kdenlivetitle>
